      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To study the clinical manifestations of gastroduodenal complications, 125 patients with moderate and severe bronchial asthma were examined. The patients were divided into 2 groups: 1) 58 patients without gastroduodenal complications and 2) 67 patients with such complications. The examination has revealed that gastroduodenal pathology more frequently develop in patients with severe steroid-dependent bronchial asthma, which is characterized with few symptoms and a latent course."},
